comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T05:13:54.247Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses and all existing milestones for MCP 2026-07-28 interoperability current protocol extensions and released-artifact outcomes. pm-9rgaal proves SDK completeness but not protocol-version conformance."
body: "## Exit evidence\n\n- Canonical 2026-07-28 core and every supported extension have requirement-level owners and passing negative controls.\n- Legacy protocol support is explicit, bounded, telemetry-visible, and sunset-ready.\n- Public SDK owns semantics and both real transports are thin tested adapters.\n- Security, authorization, privacy, consent, caching, schema resource bounds, and observability gates pass.\n- Tasks, skills, and Apps are negotiated extensions and absence preserves all core functionality.\n- Packed and published npm, npx, bunx, stdio, and Streamable HTTP consumers pass the canonical agent journey.\n- Source, contracts, generated schemas, docs, discovery, package metadata, release metadata, and runtime behavior agree exactly."
